<|im_start|>user
Please identify the correct one sentence summary of the book For Whom the Bell Tolls. Please respond with only "A", "B", "C", or "D".
(A) A Hero of Our Time is a novel by Mikhail Lermontov that follows the adventures and romantic pursuits of the charismatic and enigmatic Pechorin, revealing the emptiness and moral ambiguity of the post-Napoleonic era in Russia. 
(B) For Whom the Bell Tolls is a novel by Ernest Hemingway, set during the Spanish Civil War. It follows an American volunteer, Robert Jordan, who is tasked with blowing up a bridge behind enemy lines. Along the way, he becomes deeply involved with the local guerrilla fighters, falls in love with a Spanish woman named Maria, and grapples with the complexities of war, love, and sacrifice. Through vivid descriptions and Hemingway's signature sparse prose, the novel explores themes of loyalty, courage, and the human cost of conflict.
(C) A Hero of Our Time, written by Mikhail Lermontov, is a novel that follows the adventures of the enigmatic and reckless protagonist, Pechorin, in the Caucasus region during the early 19th century. Through his encounters with various characters, including the passionate Grushenka and the idealistic Dolgorukov, Pechorin embodies the conflicted spirit of the "superfluous man," a symbol of the alienation and disillusionment experienced by many Russian intellectuals of the time. The novel explores themes of love, honor, and the search for meaning, as it delves into Pechorin's complex character and the consequences of his actions, ultimately questioning the ideals of heroism and the nature of human existence.
(D) For Whom the Bell Tolls is a novel by Ernest Hemingway that follows an American volunteer fighting alongside Spanish Republicans during the Spanish Civil War, as he becomes involved in a dangerous mission to blow up a bridge.<|im_end|>
